== About me
I am a final-year Ph.D. student in Biostatistics at Duke-NUS Medical School, supervised of Prof. [https://blog.nus.edu.sg/bibhas/ Bibhas Chakraborty], with an expected graduation in July 2025. Previously, I earned my Master's degree in Biostatistics and a dual Bachelor's degree in Medicine and Applied Mathematics from Peking University.

== Research Interest
I develop statistical and machine learning methodologies for impactful applications in digital health. My primary research interests include:

    - Sequential decision making for adaptive interventions
    - Contextual bandits and Reinforcement learning
    - Longitudinal data analysis and Causal Inference
    - Online and Adaptive experiment design



